     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Blocking memoryDump:credentialAccess and jumpHost:lateralMovement makes the target unreachable. Blocking memoryDump cuts off dbLogin and ssoLogin, which in turn cuts off backupHost, secretsManager, appServer, vaultRead and domainAdmin. Blocking jumpHost cuts off the rest: it stays reachable through vpnSession (dmzWeb plus workstation, both fed by footholds), and it is the remaining route to mailArchive, codeRepo and serviceAccount. With both blocked, every parent of crownData (mailArchive, vaultRead, dbReplica, codeRepo) is unreachable. One block is not enough. jumpHost alone still leaves dbReplica reachable via ssoLogin and appServer, and memoryDump alone still leaves jumpHost reachable via vpnSession. No other single step cuts both routes.\"}"
    }
